  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/64be2bb3-1c3e-40c4-90b0-cbe674f7f028-image.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 191px;\" /><br /><br />Consider any small element <mml:math xmlns:m=\"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/math\" xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mml:mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dl</mml:mi></mml:math> of arc of angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math> . Then magnetic force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>B</mi></math> outwards&nbsp;&nbsp;<br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/4470a766-a3dd-4fe4-adac-48a174d92892-image.png\" style=\"width: 280px; height: 208px;\" /><br /><br />For equilibrium of element&nbsp;<br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">Idl B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">T sin</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">d&#952;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />For small angle&nbsp;<math><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">sin&#952;</mi><mo>&#8771;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>l</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">B</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>T</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">Idl B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">dl</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>R</mi></math><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/64be2bb3-1c3e-40c4-90b0-cbe674f7f028-image.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 191px;\" /><br />&nbsp;",
